	(text "EYE IN THE SKY - QUADCOPTER WIRING  (ESP32 flight controller + Jetson Nano companion)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3 3)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "70d74314-4050-436d-a209-a599599e743b")
	)
	(text "Nets are joined by matching labels. Motor and I2C pins follow firmware/README.md (ESP-Drone default ESP32 pin map). Full reasoning: kicad/README.md"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7567eb50-8fc8-4e3c-bb9b-7a2a99547dfa")
	)
	(text "ESP32 PIN ASSIGNMENT (silkscreen -> GPIO -> net)\nD4  GPIO4   MOTOR_M1  front left  (firmware MOTOR01_PIN)\nD33 GPIO33  MOTOR_M2  back left   (MOTOR02_PIN)\nD32 GPIO32  MOTOR_M3  back right  (MOTOR03_PIN)\nD25 GPIO25  MOTOR_M4  front right (MOTOR04_PIN)\nD21 GPIO21  I2C0_SDA  MPU-6050 + BMP390 + INA226\nD22 GPIO22  I2C0_SCL  MPU-6050 + BMP390 + INA226\nD19 GPIO19  MPU_INT   (MPU_PIN_INT)\nVN  GPIO39  BARO_INT  BMP390 data-ready (input-only pin)\nD34 GPIO34  PWR_ALERT INA226 alert, open-drain, R1 pull-up\nD27 GPIO27  UART2 TX -> Jetson J41-10 (UART_2_RX)\nD26 GPIO26  UART2 RX <- Jetson J41-8  (UART_2_TX)\nVIN         +5V from buck    3V3 -> sensor supply\n\nI2C ADDRESSES (one bus, no clashes)\nMPU-6050 0x68 (AD0=GND)  BMP390 0x77 (SDO=3V3)  INA226 0x40\n\nNOTES\n- GPIO26/27 are the optional buzzer pins in ESP-Drone:\n  set BUZZER_ON=n in menuconfig, then use them for UART2.\n- Jetson: sudo systemctl disable nvgetty  (frees /dev/ttyTHS1).\n- Jetson 3.3V pins (1,17) left open: never tie two regulators.\n- Motor SIG is 3.3 V PWM into each motor's driver/ESC input;\n  motor V comes from VBAT (after the INA226 shunt), not the ESP32.\n- Unplug the 5V rail before connecting ESP32 USB, or vice versa.\n- Board: ESP32 DevKit V1 30-pin (DOIT layout); VIN feeds its AMS1117."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 380 40.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
